---
import Guide from "../../layouts/Guide.astro";
import { cliFilename as filename, cliRun as run, npxRun } from "../../lib/install";
---
<Guide title="Get started">
<p slot="intro">Diorama UI gives you React components as source. Use your own app, with Tailwind CSS and an <code>@/*</code> alias pointing to your source directory.</p>

<h2 id="install">Install with the CLI</h2>
<p>Run the CLI with <code>npx</code>. It installs the source and records what you installed, so later updates can distinguish upstream changes from your own edits.</p>
<pre class="code-frame">{`${npxRun} init --src src
${npxRun} add theme-zero-css font-aspekta button`}</pre>
<p><code>init</code> creates <code>ui.config.json</code>. Existing app files stay intact. Use <code>--src</code> to match your app’s source directory and configure the same alias in your framework.</p>
<p>The CLI reports any npm dependencies you need to install. Every component page shows its own <code>add</code> command, and a Markdown twin of the page for agents.</p>
<h2>Load the foundations</h2>
<p>Import <code>src/styles/theme-zero.css</code> after Tailwind. Load <code>/fonts/aspekta/aspekta.css</code>, and <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bydiorama/ui/main/registry/fonts/aspekta/AspektaVF.woff2">download the Aspekta font</a> beside it in <code>public/fonts/aspekta/</code>. Keep its OFL notice there.</p>
<h2 id="shadcn">Existing shadcn apps</h2>
<p>The shadcn CLI is an alternative. Add the namespace below to <code>components.json</code>, then install the parts you need.</p>
<pre class="code-frame">{JSON.stringify({ registries: { "@bydiorama": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bydiorama/ui/main/r/{name}.json" } }, null, 2)}</pre>
<pre class="code-frame">npx shadcn@latest add @bydiorama/button</pre>
<p>Our CLI also reads an existing <code>components.json</code>. Running <code>init</code> retains its aliases, so you can adopt the owned channel gradually.</p>
<h2 id="from-a-file">Run the CLI from a file</h2>
<p>If your project cannot reach the registry, <a href={`/downloads/${filename}`} download>download the CLI</a> into your project and run it from there. It is the same CLI and needs no repository checkout.</p>
<pre class="code-frame">{`${run} init --src src
${run} add button`}</pre>
<h2>Keep the source yours</h2>
<p>Read it, adapt it, and keep the typed documentation beside it. Use <code>sync</code> to review upstream changes before replacing code you have modified.</p>
<p><a href="/components/">Browse components</a> · <a href="/docs/agents/">Build with an agent</a> · <a href="/docs/motion/">Motion</a></p>
</Guide>
